From b3721b53ee4b96efba4485b0768ba189f10f87ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:19:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: several hard disk images, one per ACSI ID

HDDIMAGE_<id> ("path" or "path RO") attaches an image to exactly that
ACSI ID (it has to be raw; otherwise the image stays unattached, logged).
The single HDDIMAGE of before (and of the config screen) moves to the first
raw ID without an image when the settings are loaded. USB drives in raw
mode take the raw IDs that are left, as before.

settings/hddimage: "ids" (per ID: raw, path, readOnly), each image's
"id"; PUT {"attach": {path, id, readOnly}} (an image on one ID only) and
{"detach": {id | path}}; {"path", "readOnly"} as before goes to the
image's ID or the first free raw one. Delete refuses an image on any ID,
rename follows it on its ID.
